{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517373-how-to-hunt-down-a-mathuselah-advice-for-a-chronicle-finale","id":1517373,"title":"How to hunt down a Mathuselah? Advice for a Chronicle Finale","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-07T10:37:19-07:00","id":1517373,"title":"How to hunt down a Mathuselah? Advice for a Chronicle Finale","content":"I'm currently finishing a V5 Chronicle &quot;UK Red List&quot;, where my coterie is helping track down and kill or aprehend an elder of Ravnos clan. For political reasons, they are told about the small fraction of the whole operation, as are all Kindred involved so nobody can connect the dots who is the real target: Hazimel, lying in torpor underneath Sarajevo, Bosnia. Blood spilled during two wars in former Yugoslavia protected this mathuselah from Zapathasura's awakening and Week of Nightmares.<br /> Now, someone tracked Hazimel through his blood, through Khalil Ravana to be precise (Yep, he got busted in Montreal). Our coterie's employers gave them the job of getting access to Hazimel's haven.<br /> My question to You would be: How would you hunt down Mathuselah in V5 setting (I do want to use Advanced disciplines for him) through direct or less direct approach. How aware would it be of incoming danger? How many Kindred should be engaged in it? How aware Hazimel would be whilst in torpor?<br /> <br /> <i>English is not my first language so sorry for all mistakes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27765-euderos","name":"Euderos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27765_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T13:55:22-07:00","id":1517395,"title":"","content":"What can you say about the chronicle's PCs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T03:09:34-07:00","id":1517465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517373-how-to-hunt-down-a-mathuselah-advice-for-a-chronicle-finale?p=1517395#post1517395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What can you say about the chronicle's PCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I for one, if they go after Hazimel, the Rakshasa of Rakshasas?<br /> You can say about them, they are toast<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Euderos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517373-how-to-hunt-down-a-mathuselah-advice-for-a-chronicle-finale#post1517373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question to You would be: How would you hunt down Mathuselah in V5 setting (I do want to use Advanced disciplines for him) through direct or less direct approach</div> </div> </div> </div>Would &quot;use&quot; the Second Inquisition , &quot;guide them&quot; to the said Mathuselah and let them nuke the site from orbit<br /> Or a terrorist attack or a full scale war as a civer up and a few not-intentional-at-all missles will do the trick...<br /> And even then, it is totally in the realm of possibility, Hazimel would just warp Reality either with <b>Truths of the Universe</b> (Make a created illusion permanently real) or with <b>Mayaparisatya</b>: (Temporarily make an illusion completely real or alter a person or object that already exists, possibly even erasing them from existence) not to mention the lesser Chimerstry powers and Fortitude<br /> And no, he probably not Frenzy either, Animalism is there for a reason and wuold either ignore the frenzy or just would throw his Beast in to a rat or something<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Euderos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517373-how-to-hunt-down-a-mathuselah-advice-for-a-chronicle-finale#post1517373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many Kindred should be engaged in it?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Depends on the Kindred... and situation<br /> Even Monty Coven was able to kill Mithras! True, after the German Blitz of London during World War II. drove him to torport, then in 1996 a pack of angry Lupin attacked the still &quot;weak&quot; Mithras. He <i>defeated them</i>, but was exhausted and horribly wounded<br /> Only after then Monthy had a chance<br /> Mithras was realitvely &quot;young&quot; Embraced 1258 BC<br /> Hazimel? Harappan Civilisation has its earliest roots in 6000 BC and its two greatest cities, Mohenjo-daro and Harappa, emerged c. 2600 BC The Ravnos ruled Harappa and went to war against the asuratizayya stronghold of Mohenjo-Daro. The final battle reportedly lasted for a year and a night, ending when Chandraputra took the head of his millennial adversary and condemned its soul to the most horrible of the many Hells.<br /> But this was just the last straw that broke the camel back so to speak, the conflict between the Ravnos and the Kuei-jin raged AGES, just around this time Hazimel became war-weary and confronted his sire about the matter.<br /> The two became bitter enemies and Hazimel fled but eventually Zapathasura took his Eye from him and imprisoned him until he would repent.<br /> He is old as dirt and very powerfull<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Euderos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517373-how-to-hunt-down-a-mathuselah-advice-for-a-chronicle-finale#post1517373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How aware Hazimel would be whilst in torpor?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Totally<br /> Hazimel - even without his Eye - was famous about knowing everything<br /> Chandraputra even in V20 went that far to actually realse him and gave back his Eye, becasue Ravana (their brother, who bacme the Yama King of the same name) returned with his infernal hordes and was behind the renewed hostility and activity of the Kuei-Jin in India.<br /> Chandraputra, arguably one of the gratest general in history <i>needed </i>Hazimel's insight and might and was willing to but aside millenia old grudges<br /> In V5 and your chronicle? I don't know<br /> But if you took... inspiration from the previous edition, Hazimel probably know what they are planing before they were even Embraced. Or born.<br /> Thrugh the editions and novels Hazimel demonstrated quite a formidable knowladge and usage of Auspex, not limited to<br /> Lv 6. <b>Clairvoyance</b>: See what is happening in a distant location<br /> Lv 6. <b>Horoscopic Forecast</b>: Gain a glimpse of the target's future<br /> Lv 6. <b>Telepathic Communication</b>: Mentally speak with someone, even if they are a great distance away<br /> Lv 6. <b>The Dreaming</b>: Be somewhat aware of events concerning you while in torpor<br /> \u200bLv 6. <b>The Mind Revealed:</b> Continuously read someone's thoughts to know what they are thinking and about to do<br /> Lv 7. <b>Pluck the Secret</b>: Learn what a target knows about a specific subject<br /> Lv 7.<b> Stealing the Mind's Eye:</b> See and hear what a target does and even use some Disciplines through them<br /> Lv 7. <b>Supernal Awareness</b>: Sense events and deeds anywhere in the world\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> Lv 8. <b>Omniscience</b>: Learn the personalities and identities of all creatures around you<br /> Lv 8. <b>Psychic Assault: </b>Make a powerful mental attack against a target's psyche<br /> Lv 8. <b>The Oracle's Sight:</b> Hear and see the thoughts of everyone around you<br /> Lv 9. <b>False Slumber</b>: Astrally project while in torpor<br /> Lv 9. <b>Precognition: Gain </b>some insight as to what may happen at a particular time and place<br /> Lv 9. <b>Sight of the Oracle</b>: Always know what is happening around you, gain visions of past and future events, and increase other supernatural senses<br /> And these are just the ones you can deduce from clan novel Ravnos - but even if you use the Lv 6. powers? Yeah...<br /> He.<br /> Would.<br /> Be.<br /> Aware.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T05:45:21-07:00","id":1517475,"title":"","content":"Sure. It's an Anarch coterie hired by an Independent Clan. There is 10th Gen Banu Haqim prison guard, 10th Gen Gangrel head hunter, 10th Gen Malkavian antique collector, 11th Gen Ministry &quot;Hummanitarian Doctor&quot; and 10th Gen Nosferatu Masquerade fixer. Banu Haqim is warrior/rogue, Gangrel is a tank/scout, Malk serves as ears to their employer, Ministry is a social rogue (Corruption corruption!!!), and Nosferatu is obsessed with figuring out who wants what in this contract. Also he keeps the rest of the coterie up to date with internet, as all of them were ambraced in the first 25 years of 20th century.<br /> They all have Blood Potency 2, and almost 100 years as a Kindred at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27765-euderos","name":"Euderos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27765_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T05:49:41-07:00","id":1517476,"ti