br /> Mithras was realitvely &quot;young&quot; Embraced 1258 BC<br /> Hazimel? Harappan Civilisation has its earliest roots in 6000 BC and its two greatest cities, Mohenjo-daro and Harappa, emerged c. 2600 BC The Ravnos ruled Harappa and went to war against the asuratizayya stronghold of Mohenjo-Daro. The final battle reportedly lasted for a year and a night, ending when Chandraputra took the head of his millennial adversary and condemned its soul to the most horrible of the many Hells.<br /> But this was just the last straw that broke the camel back so to speak, the conflict between the Ravnos and the Kuei-jin raged AGES, just around this time Hazimel became war-weary and confronted his sire about the matter.<br /> The two became bitter enemies and Hazimel fled but eventually Zapathasura took his Eye from him and imprisoned him until he would repent.<br /> He is old as dirt and very powerfull<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> Totally<br /> Hazimel - even without his Eye - was famous about knowing everything<br /> Chandraputra even in V20 went that far to actually realse him and gave back his Eye, becasue Ravana (their brother, who bacme the Yama King of the same name) returned with his infernal hordes and was behind the renewed hostility and activity of the Kuei-Jin in India.<br /> Chandraputra, arguably one of the gratest general in history <i>needed </i>Hazimel's insight and might and was willing to but aside millenia old grudges<br /> In V5 and your chronicle? I don't know<br /> But if you took... inspiration from the previous edition, Hazimel probably know what they are planing before they were even Embraced. Or born.<br /> Thrugh the editions and novels Hazimel demonstrated quite a formidable knowladge and usage of Auspex, not limited to<br /> Lv 6. <b>Clairvoyance</b>: See what is happening in a distant location<br /> Lv 6. <b>Horoscopic Forecast</b>: Gain a glimpse of the target's future<br /> Lv 6. <b>Telepathic Communication</b>: Mentally speak with someone, even if they are a great distance away<br /> Lv 6. <b>The Dreaming</b>: Be somewhat aware of events concerning you while in torpor<br /> \u200bLv 6. <b>The Mind Revealed:</b> Continuously read someone's thoughts to know what they are thinking and about to do<br /> Lv 7. <b>Pluck the Secret</b>: Learn what a target knows about a specific subject<br /> Lv 7.<b> Stealing the Mind's Eye:</b> See and hear what a target does and even use some Disciplines through them<br /> Lv 7. <b>Supernal Awareness</b>: Sense events and deeds anywhere in the world\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> Lv 8. <b>Omniscience</b>: Learn the personalities and identities of all creatures around you<br /> Lv 8. <b>Psychic Assault: </b>Make a powerful mental attack against a target's psyche<br /> Lv 8. <b>The Oracle's Sight:</b> Hear and see the thoughts of everyone around you<br /> Lv 9. <b>False Slumber</b>: Astrally project while in torpor<br /> Lv 9. <b>Precognition: Gain </b>some insight as to what may happen at a particular time and place<br /> Lv 9. <b>Sight of the Oracle</b>: Always know what is happening around you, gain visions of past and future events, and increase other supernatural senses<br /> And these are just the ones you can deduce from clan novel Ravnos - but even if you use the Lv 6. powers? Yeah...<br /> He.<br /> Would.<br /> Be.<br /> Aware.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>For me Rakshasa and Hazimel are one and the same, rebelious childe of Zarathasura (I like Indian origin of the Ravnos clan), one of many masks this mathuselah put on during his unlife. I forgot to mention, as I posted it pretty late at night: Chimestry is dead as a discipline for now, as it died with the founder of the clan. But it stil would have full access to Animalism, Fortitude and God knows what else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27765-euderos","name":"Euderos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27765_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T07:02:24-07:00","id":1517486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Euderos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517373-how-to-hunt-down-a-mathuselah-advice-for-a-chronicle-finale?p=1517476#post1517476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forgot to mention, as I posted it pretty late at night: Chimestry is dead as a discipline for now, as it died with the founder of the clan. But it stil would have full access to Animalism, Fortitude and God knows what else.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point still stands <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Probaly Hazimel would know they are coming; it wasn't a problem for him either in torpor, either imprisoned AND torpor to &quot;help&quot; Khalil<br /> Even without Chimerstry he would be a fomiadble adversary and I still thinks your players will/would be toast <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But untimately it is your chornicle, you decide what and why it will happen, if you want them to have Hazimel a snack, by all means! These are just my suggestions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Still, <i>I think</i> their best chance would be to manipulate the Second Inquisition (or some wandering Sabbat) to do the dirty job for them munch on the barely &quot;alive&quot; ancient instead of a mano a mano, quasy-honorable showdown\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T07:10:42-07:00","id":1517487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517373-how-to-hunt-down-a-mathuselah-advice-for-a-chronicle-finale?p=1517486#post1517486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My point still stands <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Probaly Hazimel would know they are coming; it wasn't a problem for him either in torpor, either imprisoned AND torpor to &quot;help&quot; Khalil<br /> Even without Chimerstry he would be a fomiadble adversary and I still thinks your players will/would be toast <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But untimately it is your chornicle, you decide what and why it will happen, if you want them to have Hazimel a snack, by all means! These are just my suggestions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Still, <i>I think</i> their best chance would be to manipulate the Second Inquisition (or some wandering Sabbat) to do the dirty job for them munch on the barely &quot;alive&quot; ancient instead of a mano a mano, quasy-honorable showdown\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a neat idea. Thank you, I knew that I needed a Badass for a Finale, as this is another chronicle based around Revival of clan Ravnos. In it, another elder/mathuselah Phaedyme needs to enrich her vitae by diablery of the last Ravnos' 4th Gen. She also has a vial of Founder's blood (plot of previous chronicle), so it seems that she herself has to roll up her sleeves, as you helped me realize how much of a problem, even in V5 this asshole can cause <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27765-euderos","name":"Euderos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27765_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T07:21:02-07:00","id":1517488,"title":"","content":"Well they always could seek Hazimel's &quot;brother&quot;, Ravana out... and make very nasty infernal deal (or several) with the Yama King (and may even be instrumental to help him regain some or all of his powers, revitalize Lanka, and bring a nuclear apocalypse he planned since Hiroshima so he could gorge himself on tainted chi to become the Demon Emperor of the Sixth Age) <br /> A little infernalism here, some mass sacrifice there. <br /> Even could toss a lovely rivlary there, after all Ravana' s general, the raksha Thratri, has tired of waiting for Ravana and has decided to rule as regent over the Yomi Hell Lanka until her master either returns to his senses...<br /> ... or is destroyed<br /> And she maybe would hasten that destruction<br /> True, a HUGE detour of V5 but is always fun to let the party doom themseleves... err.... be crative when it comes to solutions<br /> <br /> But yeah<br /> The likes of Hazimel in V5 are... problematic to say the least","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T15:15:25-07:00","id":1517519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517373-how-to-hunt-down-a-mathuselah-advice-for-a-chronicle-finale?p=1517488#post1517488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well they always could seek Hazimel's &quot;brother&quot;, Ravana out... and make very nasty infernal deal (or several) with the Yama King (and may even be instrumental to help him regain some or all of his powers, revitalize Lanka, and bring a nuclear apocalypse he planned since Hiroshima so he could gorge himself on tainted chi to become the Demon Emperor of the Sixth Age)<br /> A little infernalism here, some mass sacrifice there.<br /> Even could toss a lovely rivlary there, after all Ravana' s general, the raksha Thratri, has tired of waiting for Ravana and has decided to rule as regent over the Yomi Hell Lanka until her master either returns to his senses...<br /> ... or is destroyed<br /> And she maybe would hasten that destruction<br /> True, a HUGE detour of V5 but is always fun to let the party doom themseleves... err.... be crative when it comes to solutions<br /> <br /> But yeah<br /> The likes of Hazimel in V5 are... problematic to say the least</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I don't know much about Ravana's whereabouts after he left sir Sire. What are your sources? It's intersting as hell man!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27765-euderos","name":"Euderos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27765_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T23:40:21-07:00","id":1517539,"title":"","content":"Duplicate via f\u00f3rum flag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 07-11-2023, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T23:41:22-07:00","id":1517540,"title":"","content":"Okay, so it was either too large, or simply the forum hates me, I will try to post again, if it not helps...?<br /> Well you have to wait my answer ot be approved by Forum <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Let's try again!<br /> <br /> Clanbook: Ravnos Revised details the Karavalanisha Vrana, translated as Wounds of the Night's Sword.<br /> In the Holy text of the indian Ravnos, the god's appointed protectors of humanity, the siddhittizaya, had been corrupted by the demons they were charged to fight and had taken to devouring the flesh, blood, and souls of mortals. Outraged, the gods cursed them, naming them asuratizayya or &quot;countless demons&quot; and declaring that from now on they would only find sustenance in devouring flesh and blood. This only encouraged the asuratizayya, however, who embraced their sins and gorged on humanity.<br /> <br /> In Kindred of the East the Wan Xian, the &quot;Ten Thousand Heroes&quot; were chosen by the August Personage of Jade (the mightiest Minsiter of Heaven, leader of the heavly order and heavenly bureaucracy, the only one who is above the Scarlet Phoneix/Queen and the Ebon Dragon, aka. God basically) to guide and protect the universe in ancient history. The Wan Xian were originally chosen by tests of skill and courage, and fed on the ambient chi of the universe. However, they fell from grace, learning to feed off of the chi of living beings and corrupting the tests of worthiness. Their children, the Jin Hai tried to keep them on the path of righteousness, but were eventually killed for their presumption. As the blood of the Golden Children cooled, the August Personage pronounced judgement on His former champions. He cursed them to live as undead, unable to acquire chi except from drinking the blood of the living, and to exist in a brutal mockery of their former state. He revised the tests so that the former heroes and champions were replaced by criminals and murderers who escaped from Hell itself. Then He left the Wan Kuei alone to contemplate their crimes.<br /> <br /> The two connects<br /> The siddhittizaya of the Ravos were the Wan Xian, the &quot;Ten Thousand Heroes&quot; and became the asuratizayya, the Wan Kuei (later Kuei-Jin) the Ten Thousand Demons&quot;<br /> Checks out<br /> <br /> <br /> Back to Clanbook: Ravnos Revised and the Karavalanisha Vrana.<br /> Dismayed by this turn of events, the gods agreed to create a foe that would make the asuratizayya know true terror and curtail their gluttony. To that end, the gods took the soul of the man most grievously wronged by the asuratizayya and gave him new life, making him a monster so that he and his descendants might hunt the asuratizayya. Though many of the gods bestowed him with great gifts to further his cause, not all of them agreed to creating another dark force in the world. Three placed curses upon the man so that he should fear falling into temptation as the siddhittizaya had, and so the man would forever be threatened by the touch of fire and sunlight, and would also know an eternity of physical and spiritual hunger just as the creatures he hunted. Named Zapathasura, or &quot;accursed demon&quot;, he was then sent out to drive the infernal hordes from the world.<br /> In the centuries that followed Zapathasura supposedly Embraced five others: Black Mother, Rakshasa, Chandraputra, Ravana, and Ramessu.<br /> <br /> How many is this ture?<br /> Good question and mostly<i> don't really matter.</i><br /> Zapathasura may wrapped an elaborate myth in order to justify their existence and their claim over India (or made it a reality with Chimerstry to make it real... dealer's choice)<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, the facts are:<br /> - The Ravnos were and are a presence in India.<br /> - The city-nation of Harappa indeed, <i>historically</i> went to war against Mohenjo-Daro. Now, the Clanbook says, Harappa was a Ravnos stropnghold, while Mohenjo-Daro was asuratizayya HQ. Both source tell during the battle, the two generals called forth otherworldly aid, forced &quot;the light of four suns&quot; to shine upon each other and turned the river valley red with the blood of thousands of mortals and Kindred.<br /> The &quot;false suns&quot; are a returning motif in Clan Book: Ravnos, Land of Eight Million Dreams (Changeling the Dreaming supplement), Dragons of the East (Mage supplement) and Hengeyokai: Shapeshifters of the East (Werewolf supplement) like in the Kindred of the East supplements so... there is a very good chance, it &quot;happened&quot;<br /> - The Raktasadhu of India is the mutual alliance of the the Daitya, Danava, Nagaraja, Eastern Ravnos, and Wu Zao against the ever-posing threat of the Kuei-jin (mostly the Infinite Thunders Court of southern India and the Golden Court of eastern India.), the Camarilla, the Ashirra, the local Sabbat and the Tzimisce Methuselah Kartarirya and her Tzimsice)<br /> - The \u200bKuei-jin wete an are a presence in India, the Infinite Thunders Court of southern India and the Golden Court of eastern India<br /> - The conflict between the Ravnos and the Kuei-jin in a war, so intense, it eventually led to the Week of Nightmares. In the 1990s, the cold war between the Kuei Jin of the Infinite Thunders Court and the Ravnos of India heated up. The Ravnos eventually took a page from the Sabbat playbook and began mass-Embracing candidates, sending armies of neonates to be slaughtered by the Wan Kuei. The psychic backlash from these deaths reverberated up the lineages of the Ravnos, eventually waking Methuselahs who joined the fight, only to result in the eventual awakening of Zapathasura himself in 1999.<br /> - In the &quot;ultimate conflict&quot; between the two race, in the Week of Nightmare Zapathasura rampaged across India to Bangladesh for two days, calling its childer to it, but on the third day was attacked by three of the eldest Kuei-jin Bodhisattvas (Kuei-jin that have reached the final stages of their chosen Dharmas) Tieh Ju, the Iron Chrysanthemum, Eight Tunders Master and Chou Li (The Time of Thin Blood)<br /> <br /> So these are &quot;true&quot; and &quot;facts&quot;<br /> As for Ravana? Clanbook: Ravnos Revised details how he thrown in his lot with demons and abandoned his master, and tried tempting his Sire into infernalism. Ravana was said to bargain with true demons for power even greater than Zapathasura before disappearing<br /> Around this time the Yama King known as Ravana rose apeard and rose to power (tho' this is a bit harder to confirm, since the &quot;history&quot; regarding the the Yama Kings are murky at best. For example The Kitsune and the Nuwisha both claim Hanuman who infiltrated the Yama King's Hell was one of their own, - though the legends suggest that Hanuman was a monkey and we actually have a Hsien (or Shinma), the &quot;little gods&quot; of the Middle Kingdom legend about a Hanuman who was a Hsien - With masterful stealth, Hanuman infiltrated Lanka and, using Gifts given to him <i>specifically</i> to punish Ravana, he engulfed the whole island in cleansing fire and ruined Lanka)<br /> 1000 Hells, Hengeyokai and Land of Eight Million Dreams a bit hard to navigate when it comes to &quot;facts&quot;, but from several supplements it is more of deductable than written fact, the Yama King Rava is the Ravnos Ravana who &quot;ascended&quot; (descended) in to Yomi and carved out a Hell of his own.<br /> Ravana, the Yama King's descirption eerly match the Ravnos one actually...<br /> Besides, a vampire becoming a Demon is not unheard of, Mary the Black and Nergal/Huitzilopochtli both managed to become a Demon<br /> But a Yama King os not a Demon (or not all of them at least, in the western sense)<br /> Mikaboshi, lord of the Wicked City is another Yama King was \u200ba mortal; he was originally a Japanese scholar and fang shih who was invited by the Chinese court to be an advisor. Unfortunately, he was consumed by a lust for power, and turned to infernalism. He created many architectural configurations to develop and focus corrupted chi through the Yin world to fuel his magics, but was eventually found out, forcing him to flee into the spirit worlds permanently and became a Yama King<br /> So if a mortal could have done it with infernalism and 4th Generation Ravnos easly could have done the same (just way earlier)<br /> <br /> True, there is not 100% confirmed Ravan the Ravnos is Ravana the Yama King, I mnust admit, but I would day, according those supplements?<br /> 99% he is <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T23:42:08-07:00","id":1517541,"title":"","content":"Okay, so it was either too large, or simply the forum hates me, I tried to post again, but ran in to flagged.. again<br /> Well you have to wait my answer to be approved by Forum <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[